WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.934
-Welcome back, everybody!
I'm hanging out with Rose Byrne!

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:05.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:08.167
We know you're from Australia.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.567
You do a lot
to promote tourism there,

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:12.367
so I thought it'd be fun to play
a fun Australian-themed new game

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.300
called "Down Under
Drawing Challenge."

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.434
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:17.934
-♪ Down Under
Drawing Challenge ♪

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:21.567
-Now, we have a stack of
Australian-inspired clues, okay?

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.434
You and I are gonna take turns
picking a clue,

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:25.234
drawing it on this tablet.

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:27.868
But since it's the
"Down Under Drawing Challenge,"

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:30.300
you draw the clue,
and it'll be shown upside-down

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.767
on the screen behind us.
Once, you start drawing,

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:36.000
the other person has 25 seconds
to guess the clue, okay?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.667
Rose, since you're my guest,
why don't you draw first?

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.601
-Okay.
-Yeah, you're so lucky.

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:42.200
Yeah, here we go.
All right.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.000
-So you can't look at this.
-No, I won't look at this.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.100
You pick the clue, and I have
25 seconds to guess it.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.234
-Okay.
-All right.

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:49.834
So just draw it normal, I guess,
and I'll just --

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:51.367
-Okay.
-Let's start the clock.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.434
Go.

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.868
♪♪

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.901
Hand.
A ring.

00:00:56.901 --> 00:01:00.367
Uh...

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:03.968
Oh, crocodile!
-Yes!

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.133
-Is that right?
-Yes!

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.133
[ Dings ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.434
I cheated a little bit,
but it's right.

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.267
Very well done.
-Oh, it's upside down.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:12.667
-Upside down
it even looked good.

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.200
Even upside down I loved it.
-Okay.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.801
-All right, here we go.
I'm gonna clear this one.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:18.968
-Aww, croc.
-Well done, well done.

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:20.234
Okay.
-Okay.

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.334
-Here we go --
-So, now I look here?

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:23.367
-Yeah, or you can
look back here.

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.000
It doesn't matter.
Okay, here we go.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.701
Okay.

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:28.133
♪♪

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:29.367
-Mm.

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:31.567
Well, I don't know
what that looks like, but...

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:35.634
Oh, it's a person.
Upside-down person

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:38.300
in a pond...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.367
...with a -- with a tree
over the top of them...

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.133
[ Laughter ]
...and they --

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:45.000
Yeah, it's a tree.
It's a tree.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.501
Oh, it's a wave!
Oh, it's a wave!

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:48.834
They're surfing.
-Yes, it is! Yes!

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:51.033
[ Dings ]
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:53.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.567
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:59.767
-I keep forgetting
it's upside down behind me.

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:01.667
I'm like, "How are you
not getting this?

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:04.100
Yeah, but...
"It's clearly --" Okay.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.801
All right, this is yours.
Yeah.

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:06.901
Here we go, bud.
-Okay.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:08.534
-I'm not looking,
but then I'll look.

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:09.934
-Okay.
All right.

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.133
-Yep.
-Okay.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:12.968
-25, go.
-Okay.

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.334
♪♪

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.701
Nothing. Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:18.167
Hair.
Hairpiece.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:21.000
Oh, it's upside down.
Flames.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.367
Bonfire.
Uh, uh...

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:25.701
It's water again?
The Loch Ness Monster?

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:27.868
-No.
-A boat.

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:30.367
-No!
-No. I know, but upsi--

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:32.234
Teeth?
Oh, wait. The sun.

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:34.000
Oh, it's mountains.
A wave?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.300
-No!
-A storm.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.634
-No.
-It's lightning.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.067
It's a -- no.

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:41.501
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:44.033
-That's a really bad drawing.
-Oh, is that the Opera House?

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:47.601
-Yeah.
-That was very hard.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:50.667
How would I -- Of course,
Australian-themed clues.

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:54.067
-No, that's not your fault.
-No, that's fantastic!

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:56.667
-No, I bombed that.
-Audience says yes.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:57.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:00.767
I forgot --
I forgot it was Aus--

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:03.200
-It looks like a --
-No, you were fantastic.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.467
That was actually awesome.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:06.534
I was looking at it
upside down, as well, so...

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:07.901
All right. Here we go.
-Sorry.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.567
-Australian-themed clues.
Here we go.

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:10.734
-Okay.

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:11.901
-What?

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:15.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:16.868
Wow.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:18.467
-Nothing.

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:19.934
Oh.
A fish.

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:21.901
-Mm-hmm.
-A fish.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.534
Fishy.

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:27.634
Fishy and a blobby blob blob.

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:28.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:30.734
Uh, um...

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:35.000
Birds, birds, birds, birds.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.634
Coral reef.
-Yes!

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:38.300
Yay!
[ Dings ]

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.133
Coral reef?

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:43.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:45.067
Not bad.
I'm proud of my --

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:46.767
-That was really hard.
-That's not bad.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:50.167
That's pretty good. That's
a good coral reef, friend.

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:51.634
-This last one here, bud.

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:54.667
I'm gonna give you one, as well.
-Okay.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.100
We'll both draw
at the same time, okay?

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.534
And we're gonna see
if we can get Questlove

00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:00.968
to guess what we're drawing.
Okay, bud?

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:02.200
-Okay.
-Ready?

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.400
-Okay.
-Me and you will draw

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.734
the same thing.
-Oh.

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:07.667
-I know.
It's kind of...

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:09.334
-All right.
Okay, okay.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:10.868
-All right.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:14.033
-All right.
-Oh, my God.

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:16.667
Are we doing this together?
-Yeah, that's me.

00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:20.701
-Is that Harbor Bridge?
-Oh, my God.

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:25.567
Bondi Beach?
-No.

00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:27.100
-Wait.
Is this upside down?

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.067
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:32.133
-I thought we were
drawing it separately.

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:33.834
-That's not a knife.

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:36.634
[ Laughter ]
-No, it's not that --

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:39.000
[ Buzzer ]
Oh, my God!

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.667
Were we even close?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.567
How about look at it right-side
up and see what it is.

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:46.067
-Shrimp --
-Yeah.

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:48.334
-Is that shrimp on the barbie?
-Yes!

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:49.334
[ Dings ]
-Whoa!

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:50.801
-That is shrimp on a barbie!

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:53.400
♪♪

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.634
Nice!
Shrimp on the barbie!

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:57.901
Rose Byrne, everybody!
-Oh, my God.

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:59.567
Hey, if you're planning
your next vacation,

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.767
be sure to check out
Australia.com.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:02.934
We love Australia.

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.133
We'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:05.133
Stick around.

